course: dictionary
lesson: 10467
title: Tuesday and the days of the week
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tuesday is the day of the week after Monday and before Wednesday. Its place in the week is its context, so if you know the order, you know where Tuesday sits. «Mr Hughes has a cold» on Monday, «is really ill» on Tuesday, and «is in hospital» on Wednesday. The story gets worse day by day, and Tuesday comes in the middle.
explain: Tuesday is a noun, and its plural is Tuesdays. Watch the small words in front. «On Tuesday» means one particular day, while «on Tuesdays» means every Tuesday, like a club that meets each week. «Next Tuesday» and «last Tuesday» point forward or back in time.
explain: Counting helps. If Monday is 1, then Tuesday is 2, and the day after the day after Tuesday is Thursday. Use the order to check your answer: if a timetable says Tuesday, the day before is Monday and the day after is Wednesday.
fact: Tuesday is the day of the week after Monday and before Wednesday.
fact: «On Tuesday» means one particular Tuesday, and «on Tuesdays» means every Tuesday.
fact: Two days add up to two days in all: one day plus one day gives two days in all.
fact: The days of the week run in order: Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, and so on up to Sunday.
exercise: «Mr Hughes has a cold on Monday, but he is really ill on Tuesday.» Which day comes before Tuesday? | Wednesday | *Monday | Sunday | Thursday
exercise: What is the day after the day after Tuesday? | Wednesday | Monday | Friday | *Thursday
exercise: Ella's club meets «on Tuesdays». What does «on Tuesdays» mean? | Only on one Tuesday in the year | Last Tuesday only | Two days in all | *Every Tuesday
test: «Mr Hughes is in hospital on Wednesday.» Which day is the day before Wednesday? | Thursday | *Tuesday | Monday | Sunday
test: If Monday is day 1, which number is Sunday? | 5 | 8 | *7 | 6
exam: Mum's good news came «one Tuesday», and the family cheered. Which day comes just after Tuesday? | Friday | *Wednesday | Monday | Thursday
